plitting\\\":{\\\"percentBegin\\\":10,\\\"percentEnd\\\":60}}\"</code>\n               </p>\n            </li>\n         </ul>", "smithy.api#required" => {}}))
    CreateDataSourceFromRedshiftInput.add_member(:role_arn, Smithy::Schema::Shapes::ShapeRef.new(shape: RoleARN, location_name: 'RoleARN', traits: {"smithy.api#documentation" => "<p>A fully specified role Amazon Resource Name (ARN). Amazon ML assumes the role on behalf of the user to create the following:</p>\n        \n           <ul>\n            <li>\n               <p>A security group to allow Amazon ML to execute the <code>SelectSqlQuery</code> query on an Amazon Redshift cluster</p>\n            </li>\n            <li>\n               <p>An Amazon S3 bucket policy to grant Amazon ML read/write permissions on the <code>S3StagingLocation</code>\n               </p>\n            </li>\n         </ul>", "smithy.api#required" => {}}))
    CreateDataSourceFromRedshiftInput.add_member(:compute_statistics, Smithy::Schema::Shapes::ShapeRef.new(shape: ComputeStatistics, location_name: 'ComputeStatistics', traits: {"smithy.api#default" => false, "smithy.api#documentation" => "<p>The compute statistics for a <code>DataSource</code>. The statistics are generated from the observation data referenced by \n            a <code>DataSource</code>. Amazon ML uses the statistics internally during <code>MLModel</code> training.\n           This parameter must be set to <code>true</code> if the <code>DataSource</code> needs to\n          be used for <code>MLModel</code> training.</p>"}))
